      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name came from a misread message: “G” for Glavizer and “R” for Rider, which locals interpreted as Garwin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garwin%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Garwin’s early settlers included landowners George Rider and John Galvizer, who sold their land to establish the new town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garwin%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city’s first post office opened in 1880, the same year Garwin was officially platted.",
